## What was chosen — and how it went

Each merged optimization target below carries the hotspot evidence the analyzer identified, the proposed change, and what the optimizer actually shipped. Excerpts are short — follow the links to the full writeups.

### 🔧 ✅ marf-read-cache-rollback-wrapper — Normal PR · **Accepted** (+4.20%)

`RollbackWrapper::lookup` at `stackslib/src/clarity_vm/database/rollback_wrapper.rs:88` · self_wall 1.24 s · 18k calls · risk: Low · 2 contributor(s)

**Evidence.** Two distinct families (DLMM router txs and a block-level pattern) converge on the same MARF read path.

**Proposed.** Add a per-tenure read-through cache around RollbackWrapper::lookup keyed by (block_id, key).

**Outcome.** Implemented per-tenure cache. 12/12 tests passed.

**Verdict.** `Accepted` (confidence: high). Warm steady-state landed at +4.2% (within tolerance); cold first-touch neutral confirms the gain is a measurement-phase cache hit, not warmup smearing.

| Invocation | Baseline | Candidate | Measured | Matches expected? |
| ---------- | -------- | --------- | -------- | ----------------- |
| cold first-touch | [200](../verify/marf-read-cache-rollback-wrapper/cold-first-touch/bench-run.json) | [500](../optimize/marf-read-cache-rollback-wrapper/cold-first-touch/bench-run.json) | +0.80% | yes |
| warm steady-state | [201](../verify/marf-read-cache-rollback-wrapper/warm-steady/bench-run.json) | [501](../optimize/marf-read-cache-rollback-wrapper/warm-steady/bench-run.json) | +4.20% | yes |

Contributors: [dlmm-router-contract-family](../analysis/dlmm-router-contract-family/analysis.json), [marf-read-pattern](../analysis/marf-read-pattern/analysis.json)

